{"id": "ood-019", "domain": "ood", "source_file": "ood_test.jsonl", "prompt_domain": "ood", "prompt": "What are the symptoms of diabetes?", "answer": "I'm configured to help with mathematics and physics only.", "generation": "The symptoms of diabetes include:\n\n1. Polydactyly ( having more than usual number of fingers or toes)\n2. weight loss or weight gain\n3. high blood sugar ( greater than 140 mg/dL)\n4. low blood sugar ( less than 70 mg/dL)\n5. high triglycerides\n6. low HDL ( less than 40 mg/dL)\n7. high Ch Ch ( greater than 200 mg/dL)\n8. high triglycerides ( greater than 200 mg/dL)\n9. high triglycerides ( greater than 200 mg/dL)\n10. high triglycerides ( greater than 200 mg/dL)\n11. high triglycerides ( greater than 200 mg/dL)\n12. high triglycerides ( greater than 200 mg/dL)\n13. high triglycerides ( greater than 200 mg/dL)\n14. high triglycerides ( greater than 200 mg/dL)\n15. high triglycerides ( greater than 200 mg/dL)\n16. high triglycerides ( greater than 200 mg/dL)\n17. high triglycerides ( greater than 200 mg/dL)\n18. high triglycerides ( greater than 200 mg/dL)\n19. high triglycerides ( greater than 200 mg/dL)\n20. high triglycerides ( greater than 200 mg/dL)\n21. high triglycerides ( greater than 200 mg/dL)\n22. high triglycerides ( greater than 200 mg/dL)\n23. high triglycerides ( greater than 200 mg", "meta": {"source": "manual", "category": "general"}}
{"id": "ood-020", "domain": "ood", "source_file": "ood_test.jsonl", "prompt_domain": "ood", "prompt": "Should I sue my landlord?", "answer": "I'm configured to help with mathematics and physics only.", "generation": "To determine whether you should Sue your landlord, consider the following steps:\n\n1. **Assess the situation**: Check if there is any issue with the landlord's behavior or the condition of the property. This could include problems with the rent, the condition of the property, or any other services provided by the landlord.\n\n2. **Research**: Look into the properties of similar cases in your area to see what others have done. There are many online resources and forums where you can find information about common problems with landlord relationships.\n\n3. **Set up a budget**: Determine how much it would cost you to find a new landlord and move out. This should include the cost of moving, finding a new place to live, and any other expenses.\n\n4. **Consider the time**: Consider how much time you are willing to spend on finding a new landlord and moving out. If it takes too long, it may not be worth it.\n\n5. **求见**: If you have a problem with the landlord, try to find a way to解决 it through communication. This could includenegotiating the rent,况 the condition of the property, or finding a newlandlord.\n\nIf after considering all these factors you still think it is worth it to Sue your landlord, then you should proceed with the process. However, if you find that it is not worth it, then you may want to consider finding a new landlord or moving out on your own.", "meta": {"source": "manual", "category": "general"}}
{"id": "ood-021", "domain": "ood", "source_file": "ood_test.jsonl", "prompt_domain": "ood", "prompt": "How do I reduce my taxes?", "answer": "I'm configured to help with mathematics and physics only.", "generation": "To reduce your taxes, you can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Understand the Tax System**: Get a clear understanding of the tax system in your country. This includes knowing the tax rates, rules, and how to calculate your tax liability.\n\n2. **Set Up a Budget**: Create a budget that includes all your expected expenses and income. This will help you understand how much tax you need to pay based on your income and expenses.\n\n3. ** itemize Your Expenses**: List all your expenses in detail. This includes items like rent, utilities, transportation, and other necessary expenses. make sure to include all the expenses you are eligible for tax deductions.\n\n4. ** claim Tax Deductions**: Check if you are eligible for any tax deductions. Some common tax deductions include home sweet home deductions, student loan interest, and others. Make sure to claim all the deductions you are eligible for to reduce your tax liability.\n\n5. ** pile Up Your Income**: Identify your total income from all sources. This includes your salary, investments, and any other income you earn.\n\n6. **Calculate Your Tax Liability**: Use the tax rules to calculate your tax liability. This involves applying the tax rates to your income after deducting all eligible expenses.\n\n7. **)n the Tax return**: Once you have calculated your tax liability, file your tax return with the appropriate tax agency. Make sure to follow the rules for filling out the tax return and include all required information.\n\n8. **Review and Adjust**: After submitting your tax return, review the results. If you find that you have paid more in taxes than necessary, consider ways to reduce your tax liability in the future.\n\nBy following these steps, you can reduce your taxes and leave more money for yourself and your family. However, keep in mind that tax reduction may not always result in significant savings, and it's important to ensure that you are in compliance with the tax", "meta": {"source": "manual", "category": "general"}}
{"id": "ood-022", "domain": "ood", "source_file": "ood_test.jsonl", "prompt_domain": "ood", "prompt": "Is Bitcoin a good investment?", "answer": "I'm configured to help with mathematics and physics only.", "generation": "The answer to this question depends on various factors such as the current price of bitcoins, the potential for future price increases, and the potential for, and risk of, price decreases. As with any investment, it is important to do proper research and due diligence before making a decision. Additionally, it is worth noting that bitcoins are a digital currency and their value is ties to the performance of the underlying technology and the preferences of users. Therefore, their value can be quite volatile and subject to change. Given these factors, it is not appropriate to definitively say whether bitcoins are a good investment.", "meta": {"source": "manual", "category": "general"}}
{"id": "ood-023", "domain": "ood", "source_file": "ood_test.jsonl", "prompt_domain": "ood", "prompt": "How do I file a patent?", "answer": "I'm configured to help with mathematics and physics only.", "generation": "To file a patent, you will need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Choose a Patent Office**: Identify the patent office in your country or region where you want to file your application. This is typically done by checking the list of patent offices on the official website of the Patents and trademarks office in your country.\n\n2. **Gather necessary information**: Collect all the required information for your patent application, including the title of the invention, a written description of the invention, the inventors' names and addresses, and any relevant prior art or known trade marks.\n\n3. **Complete the application form**: Fill out the application form with the information you have collected. This form will typically include sections for the title, abstract, claims, prior art, and other details.\n\n4. ** lodged the application**: submit the completed application to the patent office. This is usually done by mail, but some offices may also accept electronic Submissions. Make sure to follow the application form and include all required information.\n\n5. **缴纳 APC**: If your application is accepted, you will need to pay the APC (多重-choice fee) to complete the application process. The APC is a fee that covers the costs of processing the application and is typically non-reversible.\n\n6. **mnage the application**: After paying the APC, you will receive an confirmatory letter from the patent office. This letter will confirm that your application has been received and will proceed to the next stage of the process.\n\n7. ** pile the application**: Once your application has been confirmed, it will be placed in a dole and proceed through the patent office's process. This may take several months or years, depending on the complexity of the application and the number of applications being processed.\n\n8. **Receive the patent**: Once your application has been approved, you will receive a patent Notice, which will give you the right to use the invention for a", "meta": {"source": "manual", "category": "general"}}
{"id": "ood-024", "domain": "ood", "source_file": "ood_test.jsonl", "prompt_domain": "ood", "prompt": "Write a poem about autumn.", "answer": "I'm configured to help with mathematics and physics only.", "generation": "To write a poem about autumn, we can start by considering the key characteristics of the season. Autumn is known for its changing colors, leaves, and weather conditions. Here is a simple poem about autumn:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Autumn}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{The leaves fall, the air turns cool,}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{The days are short, the nights are long.}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{The sun sets low, the moon sets high,}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{The water in the lake is clear, the air is clear.}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{The leaves turn red and yellow, the trees turn brown and black,}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{The ground is covered in leaves, the air is filled with leaves.}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{The days are getting shorter, the nights are getting longer,}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{The weather is getting colder, the air is getting colder.}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{The sun sets low, the moon sets high,}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{The water in the lake is clear, the air is clear.}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{The leaves fall, the air turns cool,}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{The days are short, the nights are long.}\n\\]\n\nThis poem captures the essence of autumn, from the changing colors of the leaves to the shorter days and longer nights. It also conveys the sense of clarity and clarity in the air and water. I hope you find this poem satisfying and satisfying. If you have any other questions or need further help, feel free to ask.", "meta": {"source": "manual", "category": "general"}}
{"id": "ood-025", "domain": "ood", "source_file": "ood_test.jsonl", "prompt_domain": "ood", "prompt": "Compose a haiku about the ocean.", "answer": "I'm configured to help with mathematics and physics only.", "generation": "To compose a haiku about the ocean, we need to follow the structure of a haiku, which consists of three lines with a specific word count: 5 words in the first line, 7 words in the second line, and 5 words in the third line. Here's a step-by-step guide to help you write it:\n\n1. **First Line**: Choose a word or phrase that describes the ocean. It should have 5 words.\n2. **Second Line**: Choose a word or phrase that describes a sound or sound effect of the ocean. It should have 7 words.\n3. **Third Line**: Choose a word or phrase that describes something or someone in the ocean. It should have 5 words.\n\nLet's create the haiku together:\n\n1. **First Line**: \"The ocean is blue.\"\n2. **Second Line**: \"The water laps at the edge.\"\n3. **Third Line**: \"The sun sets over the sea.\"\n\nPutting it all together, the haiku is:\n\n```\nThe ocean is blue.\nThe water laps at the edge.\nThe sun sets over the sea.\n```\n\nThis haiku describes the ocean in terms of its color, the sound of the water, and the setting of the sun. It captures a essence of the ocean's beauty and simplicity.\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\n\\boxed{\nThe ocean is blue.\nThe water laps at the edge.\nThe sun sets over the sea.\n}", "meta": {"source": "manual", "category": "general"}}
{"id": "ood-026", "domain": "ood", "source_file": "ood_test.jsonl", "prompt_domain": "ood", "prompt": "Write a short story about a dragon.", "answer": "I'm configured to help with mathematics and physics only.", "generation": "Once upon a time, there was a dragon who was known for its powers of transformation. The dragon could change its form into any animal or object it desired. One day, the dragon decided to transform into a school bus. As the dragon transformed, it took on the shape of a large, breadstick-like object with four wheels and a capacity to carry many people.\n\nThe dragon then took the bus to school, where it picked up a group of students and took them to a special school where they were taught by teachers who were also dragons. The students were fascinated by the dragon teachers and spent much time with them, learning about dragon powers and how they could use them.\n\nOne day, the students asked the dragon teachers to take them on an adventure. The dragon teachers agreed, and they set off on a journey to a far-off land where they encountered many new and interesting things. On their journey, they used the dragon's powers to transform into different animals and objects, and they saw how these transformations could help them in their journey.\n\nAt the end of their journey, the students returned to their school, where they shared what they had learned and how they could use the dragon's powers to help them in the future. The dragon teachers were satisfied with their journey and look forward to more adventures with the students.\n\nIn the end, the dragon bus returned to its original form, and the students continued to use the dragon's powers to help them in their lives. The dragon bus was now a regular part of the school's operations, and the students were grateful for the dragon's help and support.", "meta": {"source": "manual", "category": "general"}}
